VALUES ('kodagu', 'Kodagu (Coorg)', 'kodagu', 'ಕೊಡಗು', 'Malnad', 'Malnad', 'The Scotland of India & Coffee Capital', 'Nestled amidst misty green Western Ghats slopes, Kodagu is renowned for sprawling coffee estates, rushing waterfalls, rich Kodava martial culture, and spice plantations.', 'Madikeri', 'October to March', '2 - 4 Days', 'Cool mountain breeze, lush monsoons (June-Sept), pleasant winters (14°C - 26°C)', 12.4244, 75.7382, '{"Coffee Tasting","Waterfall Treks","Kodava Cuisine","Viewpoints"}', 5, '{"imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/17/Tadiandamol_Valley%2C_Western_Ghats.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tadiandamol_Valley,_Western_Ghats.jpg","photographer":"Wikimedia Commons / Jyotirmoy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikimedia Commons / CC BY-SA 4.0","placeId":"kodagu"}', '{"coorg-abbey-falls","coorg-rajas-seat","coorg-dubare-elephant-camp","coorg-talakaveri","coorg-madikeri-fort"}')
