VALUES ('dakshina-kannada', 'Dakshina Kannada (Mangaluru)', 'dakshina-kannada', 'ದಕ್ಷಿಣ ಕನ್ನಡ', 'Coastal', 'Coastal', 'Coastal Metropolis, Sacred Shrines & Culinary Paradise', 'A vibrant coastal district where the Netravati and Gurupura rivers meet the Arabian Sea. Renowned for red-tile heritage, Mangalorean Ghee Roast, serene beaches, and historic temples.', 'Mangaluru', 'October to February', '2 - 3 Days', 'Coastal warmth, balmy evenings, festive seafood seasons', 12.9141, 74.856, '{"Neer Dosa & Seafood","Beach Sunsets","Temple Heritage","River Cruises"}', 4, '{"imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/23/Panambur_Beach_Mangalore.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panambur_Beach_Mangalore.jpg","photographer":"Wikimedia Commons / CodePanda","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikimedia Commons / CC BY-SA 4.0","placeId":"dakshina-kannada"}', '{"dk-panambur-beach","dk-kadri-manjunatha","dk-tannirbhavi-beach","dk-pilikula"}')
