VALUES ('hassan', 'Hassan (Belur & Halebidu)', 'hassan', 'ಹಾಸನ', 'South Karnataka', 'South Karnataka', 'Epitome of Hoysala Sculptural Brilliance', 'A historical goldmine containing the intricately carved 12th-century star-shaped soapstone temples of Belur and Halebidu, alongside the towering monolith Gommateshwara statue at Shravanabelagola.', 'Hassan', 'October to March', '2 - 3 Days', 'Gentle plateau climate with comfortable mornings and evenings', 13.0033, 76.1004, '{"Hoysala Carvings","Gommateshwara Pilgrimage","Star Temple Architecture","Village Trails"}', 4, '{"imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0a/The_Courtyard_of_Chennakesava_Temple_-_Belur.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Courtyard_of_Chennakesava_Temple_-_Belur.jpg","photographer":"Wikimedia Commons / Bikashrd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikimedia Commons / CC BY-SA 4.0","placeId":"hassan"}', '{"hsn-belur-temple","hsn-halebidu-temple","hsn-shravanabelagola","hsn-shettihalli-church"}')
